Every repository of the chain is held to one code standard, and every line
of it is held to the standard: old code passes the same checks as new code.

- **Ruff** selects $rules, the high-confidence security checks
  $security and the banned-API rule $banned_api_rule (see *Banned APIs*),
  with `ignore = []` and no per-file ignores, over $trees; `ruff format`
  formats it, $line_length columns wide.
- **mypy** is strict (Python $python_version) over $trees. A test function
  may leave its fixtures unannotated where `pyproject.toml` allows it, but
  its body is still checked; only a named third-party module that ships no
  types may be imported untyped, with the reason beside it.
- **complexipy** allows no function above $max_complexity, over $trees,
  with no snapshot of old offenders.
- **Coverage** is $fail_under % of lines and branches, reached by a test
  that makes each case happen. The only exclusions are $exclude_also; there
  is no `omit`.
- **Every warning is an error** (`filterwarnings = $filterwarnings`): ours
  are fixed, not filtered.
- **No suppression comment**: no `# noqa`, `# pragma: no cover`,
  `# fmt: off`, `# complexipy: ignore` or `# nosec`. A `# type: ignore[code]`
  only where it cannot be avoided (a test passing a wrongly typed value on
  purpose), with its error code and the reason beside it or just above.
- **No snapshot or baseline** of old findings, for any tool.

The settings behind these rules are the managed blocks of `pyproject.toml`
(between `# >>> xrddevtools sync` markers), and this section is one of the
managed blocks of this file (between `<!-- >>> xrddevtools sync` markers).
`xrddevtools sync` writes them all from the standard, kept once in xrd-devtools
(`src/xrddevtools/standard`); `xrddevtools conformance`, which CI runs,
fails if one is edited by hand. To change the standard, change it there and
run `xrddevtools sync --workspace ..` over every repository.
